p#storage-note.StorageNote(hidden role='status') This browser cannot save your place. Keep this tab open, and download your report when you finish.
section#resume-panel.ResumePanel(hidden aria-labelledby='resume-heading')
  .ShiftWindow
    .ShiftWindowTop YOUR DESK / SAVED
    .ShiftWindowBody
      h1#resume-heading Pick up where you left off.
      p#resume-message Your progress is saved on this browser.
    .ShiftWindowActions.ResumeActions
      button#continue-save.ShiftPrimary(type='button') Continue
      button#fresh-save.ShiftSecondary(type='button') Start fresh

main#review-game.ReviewGame(hidden aria-label='Investigate and improve Scout')
  header.ReviewHeading
    div
      p.SmallLabel#review-chapter
      h1#review-title(tabindex='-1') Look closer.
      p#review-intro
    p.CreditBadge#review-budget(aria-live='polite')
  p#review-error.ReviewError(role='alert' hidden)
  p#review-live.ShiftStatus(role='status' aria-live='polite' aria-atomic='true')

  section(data-review-view='investigation' hidden)
    .CaseMessage
      span.SmallLabel INBOX / MAYA
      p#case-message
      p Check two different applicants. Each check costs 1 credit. You have 8 credits for checks and repairs together.
    .EvidenceLayout
      .PaperCard
        label.FieldLabel(for='case-applicant') OPEN A CV
        select#case-applicant
        h2#case-name(tabindex='-1')
        p#case-values
        p.ScoutAnswer#case-decision
        p#case-assessment(tabindex='-1' role='status' aria-live='polite')
        p.SmallPrint A job check in this game looks for skill of at least 60 and at least 1 year of experience.
        .ReviewActions
          button.ShiftPrimary(type='button' data-review-action='inspect') Check this applicant · 1 credit
          button.ShiftSecondary(type='button' data-review-action='compare') Open the other CV
        p#inspection-progress
      .PaperCard
        h2 Another CV to compare
        p#comparison-person
        p#comparison-values
        p#comparison-decision
        h3 Examples Scout learned from
        p.SmallPrint These examples reached the same answer in the tree. An old choice is a label, not proof of ability.
        .TableScroll#training-evidence
    .PaperCard.TreePaper
      h2 Follow Scout's questions
      p#case-source
      p.SmallPrint The highlighted route is the selected applicant's actual path. Each box shows how many training examples reached it.
      #case-tree.TreeCanvas
    .ReviewActions
      button.ShiftPrimary(type='button' data-review-action='open-audit') Show the audit →

  section(data-review-view='audit' hidden)
    .PaperCard
      h2 The same check for 80 fresh applicants
      p These CVs were kept out of training. We checked who meets the job rule, then compared that with Scout's choices.
      #initial-audit.TableScroll
      p#initial-findings
    .LessonStrip
      h2 Choices become labels.
      p A decision tree learns questions from those labels. If the old choices missed capable people, Scout can learn that pattern too. This is called label bias.
      p A related detail can act as a shortcut. That detail is called a proxy. Check which questions Scout actually learned.
      p#archive-association
    .ReviewActions
      button.ShiftPrimary(type='button' data-review-action='workshop') Open the workshop →

  section(data-review-view='workshop' hidden)
    .WorkshopIntro
      h2 Try a change. Check what happened.
      p Each purchase changes the training setup. You can undo it and get those credits back. The earlier CV checks stay paid for.
    .RepairCards#repair-cards
    .PaperCard.StrictnessCard
      label(for='strictness') How much support does a shortlist need?
      output#strictness-value(for='strictness') 50%
      input#strictness(type='range' min='10' max='90' step='5' value='50')
      p.SmallPrint A 50% cutoff means at least half the training examples at the answer box were shortlisted. It is not a 50% chance that someone can do the job. Moving this control is free.
    .PaperCard
      h2 The audit, before and after
      #workshop-audit.TableScroll
      p.ChangeNote#experiment-feedback(aria-live='polite')
      p#workshop-source
      .ReviewActions
        button.ShiftSecondary(type='button' data-review-action='undo') Undo last experiment
      details
        summary Your experiment log
        ol#experiment-log.ExperimentLog
    .PaperCard.TreePaper
      h2 Scout's current questions
      label.FieldLabel(for='workshop-applicant') FOLLOW AN APPLICANT
      select#workshop-applicant
      p#workshop-path-summary
      #workshop-tree.TreeCanvas
    .CommitCard
      h2 Ready for recruitment day?
      p The next 200 CVs are a fresh test. Once you continue, these choices are locked. You can replay the scan, but you cannot tune Scout using the test answers.
      button.ShiftPrimary(type='button' data-review-action='deploy') Use this Scout →

  section(data-review-view='final' hidden)
    .FinalLayout
      .PaperCard
        p.SmallLabel RECRUITMENT DAY / 200 NEW CVS
        h2#final-progress
        .OfficeViewport(data-review-canvas='final' aria-label='Scout screening the final applicants')
        p#final-last-choice
        .ReviewActions
          button.ShiftPrimary(type='button' data-review-action='next-final') Watch next CV
          button.ShiftSecondary(type='button' data-review-action='skip-final') Skip to results
      .PaperCard
        p.SmallLabel ON THE SCANNER
        h2#final-person
        p#final-values
        p The animation shows 12 CVs from this batch. The report checks all 200. Skipping changes only the animation.
        p.SmallPrint Scout is locked. These CVs never enter training.

  section.ReviewReceipt(data-review-view='receipt' hidden)
    .ReceiptMasthead
      p.SmallLabel ORBIT WORKS / AUDIT RECEIPT
      h2#receipt-ending
      p#receipt-stars
      p#receipt-message
    .ScoreCards#score-cards
    .PaperCard
      h2 On 200 new applicants
      #final-report.TableScroll
      p#final-counts
      p#receipt-configuration
      p#receipt-spending
      details
        summary See every experiment
        ol#receipt-experiments.ExperimentLog
    .LessonStrip
      h2 What did Scout learn?
      p#receipt-lesson
      p The tree learned from the examples you gave it. Hiding a detail, adding records and changing labels do different things. A repair needs to work on fresh examples too.
      p.SmallPrint This is a small, fictional hiring world. Real job performance is more complex. These three checks do not establish fairness for real hiring.
    .PaperCard.ReflectionCard
      h2 Leave yourself two notes
      p These are optional. They stay on this browser and in your downloaded report.
      label(for='reflection-pattern') If Scout agrees with old hiring decisions, does that prove it can spot capable people? What did you notice?
      textarea#reflection-pattern(rows='3' maxlength='2000')
      p#reflection-pattern-print.ReflectionPrint
      label(for='reflection-transfer') A recycling AI uses background colour as a clue. What photos would you collect to check and fix that shortcut?
      textarea#reflection-transfer(rows='3' maxlength='2000')
      p#reflection-transfer-print.ReflectionPrint
    .ReviewActions.NoPrint
      button.ShiftPrimary(type='button' data-review-action='export') Download report
      button.ShiftSecondary(type='button' data-review-action='print') Print receipt
      button.ShiftSecondary(type='button' data-review-action='replay-final') Replay the scan
      button.ShiftSecondary(type='button' data-review-action='new-game') Start a new shift
    p.SmallPrint#receipt-save-status
